After speaking to him, Durnehviir can be found atop a dilapidated, non-functional [[Skyrim:Word Wall|word wall]] to the left of the Boneyard entrance. He will only say, ''"Speak, if you have aught to say worth the listening."''

====Summoning Durnehviir====
You will need to unlock the Summon Durnehviir shout before you can use it. The first three times you summon Durnehviir, he will teach you a word of the [[Skyrim:Soul Tear|Soul Tear]] shout.
:{|class=wikitable
!Condition!!Line
|-
|Summoning Durnehviir for the first time||''"Ah! The free air of {{hover|Nirn|Vus}} at long last. As promised, I now teach you the first word of Soul Tearing: "{{hover|Essence|Rii}}" - the essence of your enemy's life force."''
|-
|Summoning Durnehviir for the second time||''"I can feel my strength returning each time I am set free from that prison! Hear now the second word of Soul Tearing: "{{hover|Tear|Vaaz}}" - meaning to tear your enemy's soul from its living vessel."''
|-
|Summoning Durnehviir for the third time||''"You have kept your side of the bargain, now let me fulfill mine. Feel the last word of Soul Tearing within yourself: "{{hover|Zombie|Zol}}" - the unlife that results when a soul is imprisoned in dead flesh."''
|}

Summoning Durnehviir on subsequent occasions will have him say one of the following lines:
:''"I rejoice in my freedom, if only for a moment."''
:''"The skies of {{hover|Skyrim|Keizaal}} are mine again!"''
:''"You give me freedom from the enslavement of the Ideal Masters. Thank you."''

==Notes==
* When not fighting, Durnehviir will simply circle around you from the air.
* In combat, Durnehviir will use several shouts: [[Skyrim:Drain Vitality|Drain Vitality]], [[Skyrim:Frost Breath|Frost Breath]], and [[Skyrim:Soul Cairn Summon|Soul Cairn Summon]], a shout unique to Durnehviir that summons a [[Skyrim:Boneman|boneman]], a [[Skyrim:Mistman|mistman]], and a [[Skyrim:Wrathman|wrathman]] all at once.
* Durnehviir is immune to [[Skyrim:Bend Will|Bend Will]], and therefore cannot be [[Skyrim:Dragon Riding|ridden]].{{DB}}
* Durnehviir has two models and two different Base Object IDs. The ID listed on this page is for the summoned Durnehviir; the Durnehviir that is fought in the Soul Cairn has a Base Object ID of xx0030d8.
* The lost souls in the Soul Cairn may say, ''"Beware the dragon Durnehviir, destroyer of souls and harbinger of the fallen."''
* Unlike [[SR:Odahviing|Odahviing]], Durnehviir can be summoned on [[SR:Solstheim|Solstheim]].{{DB}}
* Durnehviir is the only named Dragon who fully voices most of his Shouts.
* Despite the game hinting that he is undead, Durnehviir can be healed by normal Restoration spells like [[Skyrim:Heal Other|Heal Other]], which undead are normally immune to.
* During Beyond Death, Durnehviir's Soul Cairn Summon shout summons four bonemen instead of the boneman, mistman and wrathman it summons when he uses it out in Tamriel. Additionally, the bonemen tend to be melee fighters instead of archers, like you might summon with the [[Skyrim:Conjure Boneman|particular spell]].
* "Durnehviir" is likely not his original name, due to its meaning of ("Curse Never Dying"), as he would not have been undead prior to entering the Soul Cairn.

